The crossover size \(n^{*}\) is obtained from the condition  

\[
E_{\text{straight}}(n^{*})=E_{\text{folded}}(n^{*}) .
\]

Using  

\[
E_{\text{straight}}(n)=-\frac{C}{n^{p}},\qquad 
E_{\text{folded}}(n)=-\frac{\mu^{2}}{2\alpha\bigl(R_{0}+\beta n^{1/3}\bigr)^{3}}
+\frac12\bigl(k_{0}+\gamma n\bigr)(n-n_{c})^{2},
\]

we obtain  

\[
-\frac{C}{(n^{*})^{p}}
=-\frac{\mu^{2}}{2\alpha\bigl(R_{0}+\beta (n^{*})^{1/3}\bigr)^{3}}
+\frac12\bigl(k_{0}+\gamma n^{*}\bigr)(n^{*}-n_{c})^{2}.
\]

Multiplying by \(-1\) and rearranging gives the implicit equation for the crossover size:

\[
\boxed{\;
\frac{C}{(n^{*})^{p}}
= \frac{\mu^{2}}{2\alpha\bigl(R_{0}+\beta (n^{*})^{1/3}\bigr)^{3}}
-\frac12\bigl(k_{0}+\gamma n^{*}\bigr)(n^{*}-n_{c})^{2}\; } .
\]

Equivalently, one may write it in a form that isolates \(n^{*}\) on the left‑hand side:

\[
\boxed{\;
n^{*}
= \left[
\frac{C}
{\displaystyle\frac{\mu^{2}}{2\alpha\bigl(R_{0}+\beta (n^{*})^{1/3}\bigr)^{3}}
-\frac12\bigl(k_{0}+\gamma n^{*}\bigr)(n^{*}-n_{c})^{2}}
\right]^{\!1/p}
\;}
\]

which is an implicit equation for \(n^{*}\) that can be solved numerically for any given set of parameters \(\mu,\alpha,R_{0},\beta,k_{0},\gamma,C,p\) and \(n_{c}\).

