* The first sum runs over every paddle‑wheel dimer \(i\); \(\hat{\mathbf S}_{i,1}\) and \(\hat{\mathbf S}_{i,2}\) are the two \(S=½\) Cu(II) spins in that dimer.  
* The second sum runs over all nearest‑neighbour metal sites belonging to different dimers (the four bipyridine‑linked neighbours in the square‑lattice plane).  
* The last term is the Zeeman interaction (optional for susceptibility analysis).

**Sign convention:** In the form \(\hat H=\sum J_{ij}\,\hat{\mathbf S}_{i}\!\cdot\!\hat{\mathbf S}_{j}\) a **positive** exchange constant (\(J>0\)) corresponds to **antiferromagnetic** coupling (the energy is lowered when the two spins are antiparallel).  Equivalently, if one uses the alternative convention \(\hat H=-2\sum J_{ij}\,\hat{\mathbf S}_{i}\!\cdot\!\hat{\mathbf S}_{j}\), antiferromagnetism is described by \(J_{ij}<0\).

